WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.070
- [Instructor] We are told
the graph of y is equal

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:05.850
to log base two of x is shown below,

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.630
and they say graph y is equal

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.340
to two log base two of
negative x minus three.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.820
So pause this video and have a go at it.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.300
The way to think about it
is that this second equation

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.960
that we wanna graph is really
based on this first equation

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.780
through a series of transformations.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.900
So I encourage you to
take some graph paper out

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.800
and sketch how those transformations

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.250
would affect our original graph

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.650
to get to where we need to go.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.890
All right, now let's do this together.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.430
So what we already have graphed,

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.350
I'll just write it in purple,

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:40.420
is y is equal to log base two of x.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.790
Now the difference between
what I just wrote in purple

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.880
and where we wanna go is in the first case

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.310
we don't multiply anything
times our log base two of x,

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:52.480
while in our end goal we multiply by two.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:56.120
In our first situation, we
just have log base two of x

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.530
while in here we have log base two

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.947
of negative x minus three.

00:01:01.947 --> 00:01:03.830
And in fact we could even view that

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.830
as it's the negative of x plus three.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.590
So what we could do is try to
keep changing this equation

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.720
and that's going to transform its graph

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.220
until we get to our goal.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.580
So maybe the first thing
we might want to do

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.950
is let's replace our x with a negative x.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.790
So let's try to graph y is equal

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:29.110
to log base two of negative x.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.620
In other videos we've talked about

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.600
what transformation would go on there,

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.240
but we can intuit through it as well.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.040
Now whatever value y would have taken on

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.834
at a given x-value, so for
example when x equals four

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.930
log base two of four is two,

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.420
now that will happen at negative four.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.760
So log base two of the
negative of negative four,

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.100
well that's still log base two of four,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.540
so that's still going to be two.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:56.960
And if you were to put in let's say a,

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.320
whatever was happening at one before,

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.800
log base two of one is zero,

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.270
but now that's going to
happen at negative one

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.410
'cause you take the
negative of negative one,

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:07.430
you're gonna get a one over here,

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:11.190
so log base two of one is zero.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.570
And so similarly when
you had at x equals eight

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.040
you got to three, now
that's going to happen

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.000
at x equals negative eight
we are going to be at three.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.700
And so the graph is going
to look something like

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:29.430
what I am graphing right over here.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.750
All right, fair enough.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.020
Now the next thing we might wanna do is

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:39.970
hey let's replace this
x with an x plus three,

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.090
'cause that'll get us at least,

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.570
in terms of what we're taking the log of,

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:45.930
pretty close to our original equation.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:50.840
So now let's think about y
is equal to log base two of,

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.000
and actually I should put
parentheses in that previous one

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.350
just so it's clear,

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:58.760
so log base two of not
just the negative of x,

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:03.360
but we're going to replace
x with x plus three.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.690
Now what happens if you
replace x with an x plus three?

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.960
Or you could even view x
plus three as the same thing

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.870
as x minus negative three.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.800
Well we've seen in multiple examples

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.680
that when you replace
x with an x plus three

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.890
that will shift your entire
graph three to the left.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:24.890
So this shifts, shifts three to the left.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.630
If it was an x minus three in here,

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:30.850
you would should three to the right.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.150
So how do we shift three to the left?

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:36.390
Well when the point
where we used to hit zero

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:38.410
are now going to happen
three to the left of that.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:41.170
So we used to hit it at
x equals negative one,

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:43.720
now it's going to happen
at x equals negative four.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.810
The point at which y is equal to two,

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.460
instead of happening at
x equals negative four,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.240
is now going to happen
three to the left of that

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:52.130
which is x equals negative seven,

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:56.383
so it's going to be right over there.

00:03:56.383 --> 00:04:00.560
And the point at which the
graph goes down to infinity,

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:03.330
that was happening as x approaches zero,

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.060
now that's going to happen

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.760
as x approaches three to the left of that,

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.620
as x approaches negative three,

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.900
so I could draw a little
dotted line right over here

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.620
to show that as x approaches that

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:16.800
our graph is going to approach zero.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.080
So our graph's gonna look
something, something like this,

00:04:23.418 --> 00:04:26.160
like this, this is all hand-drawn

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.210
so it's not perfectly drawn
but we're awfully close.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:31.670
Now to get from where we are to our goal,

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:34.640
we just have to multiply
the right hand side by two.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:39.640
So now let's graph y, not
two, let's graph y is equal

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:45.190
to two log base two of
negative of x plus three,

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.000
which is the exact same
goal as we had before,

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.840
I've just factored out the negative

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.640
to help with our transformations.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.450
So all that means is whatever
y value we were taking on

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:59.180
at a given x you're now going
to take on twice that y-value.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:02.540
So where you were at zero,
you're still going to be zero.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:03.700
But where you were two,

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.420
you are now going to be equal to four,

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.540
and so the graph is
going to look something,

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:14.540
something like what I
am drawing right now.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:17.930
And we're done, that's
our sketch of the graph

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:20.440
of all of this business.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.760
And once again, if you're
doing it on Khan Academy,

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:23.380
there would be a choice
that looks like this

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.713
and you would hopefully pick that one.

